  ('sensitive-api-password-leakage', 'generic', 'Sensitive data exposure', 'critical',
   'Cleartext passwords returned by unauthenticated JSON API',
   'A robots.txt-disclosed or common admin API route (e.g. /api/admin/users) returns user records with cleartext password fields without authentication.',
   'User passwords exposed in public API responses enable credential theft and account takeover.',
   'rule_ref',
   '{"rule":"sensitiveApiPasswordLeakage"}'::jsonb,
   'deep',
   '{"summary":"Never return password fields in API responses; hash credentials server-side.","steps":["Remove password columns from all JSON serializers and DTOs.","Hash passwords with bcrypt/argon2; never store or transmit cleartext.","Require authentication and authorization on every /api/admin/* route."]}'::jsonb,
   'Our /api/admin/users returns Email and Password fields without auth. Remove password from API responses, hash credentials server-side, and lock admin routes behind authentication.',
   true),
  ('sensitive-api-token-leakage', 'generic', 'Sensitive data exposure', 'high',
